{"content":[{"c":["PUL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Name given to Tiglath-pileser, the Assyrian ruler (745–727 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), when he became king of Babylon (729–727 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.15.19","r":"2Kgs.15.19","rawR":"2Kgs.15.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.15.19","value":"2Kgs.15.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 15:19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.26","r":"1Chr.5.26","rawR":"1Chr.5.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.26","value":"1Chr.5.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:26"},"). The meaning of the name is unknown, and Assyrian manuscripts do not mention it, suggesting to some scholars that Pul was Tiglath-pileser’s original name. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=TiglathPileser_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"TiglathPileser_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"TiglathPileser_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Tiglath-pileser"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. African people mentioned only in ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.66.19","r":"Isa.66.19","rawR":"Isa.66.19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.66.19","value":"Isa.66.19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 66:19"}," (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). Their connection with Tarshish and Lud has strongly suggested that Pul is a copyist’s error for Put (as in various Greek manuscripts), a people related to the Egyptians and possibly a subculture of Libyans. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=PutPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"PutPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"PutPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Put (Place)"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Pul","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 15:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.15.19","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.15.19","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.15.19"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.26","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.26","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.26"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 66:19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.66.19","rawQueryValue":"Isa.66.19","sourceRefExact":"Isa.66.19"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"5d37238185325c6139fc653635f7684da587b39cf5fff23beb574a88a6c43bd6","sourceItemName":"Pul","sourceItemOrder":310,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Pul","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pul","title":"Pul","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}